 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "Danfoss iC7 Series drives fitted with the BACnet/IP (OS7BI) or BACnet MS/TP (OS7BN) fieldbus option.",
 "summary": "Danfoss iC7 drives talk BACnet/IP over the X1/X2 Ethernet ports with the OS7BI option, or BACnet MS/TP with the OS7BN option. Both operating guides print the same fixed object list: I/O values for the integrated and general-purpose I/O, run/stop and speed reference, drive measurements and hour/energy counters, PID and multi-zone setpoints, fixed-speed pump (MPC) data, and the fieldbus control and status word bits.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Taken from section 2.7 BACnet Objects (Tables 9-14) of the iC7 BACnet/IP operating guide; the iC7 BACnet MS/TP operating guide (AQ528743911395en-010101) prints the same 141 objects with the same names and access.",
  "The description field gives the drive parameter number and index each object maps to, as printed.",
  "Objects for I/O options (General Purpose I/O, Relay Option, Temperature Measurement OC7T0) and for MPC fixed-speed pumps only carry data when that option or function is used. The AI objects with a custom-unit flag take the unit configured for the input.",
  "BV 41-50 (sleep, interlock, end of curve, no flow, dry run) are printed without access or parameter; they are listed as read-only.",
  "BO 0 and BO 1 are both printed as 'Digital Output Term 15'; names kept as printed.",
  "For AV 1-7 Danfoss prints the same parameter numbers, indexes and remarks as AI 20-24 (an apparent copy error in the guide); they are kept as printed, so don't rely on them."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Set Control Place Selection to Advanced Control/Fieldbus Control and the fieldbus reference and start sources to Fieldbus (parameter group 5.5), then write BV 1 RUN/STOP Command and AV 1 Fieldbus Speed Reference 1. Read Running (BV 33), Motor Speed (AV 3), current and power, and the Trip/Warning flags with Fault Status Word 1 for alarms.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "RUN/STOP Command",
    "why": "Run/stop command (1 = run)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1",
    "name": "Fieldbus Speed Reference 1 (Input Reference 1)",
    "why": "Speed reference, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 30",
    "name": "Multi Zone Reference 1 (Setpoint 1)",
    "why": "Setpoint 1 when the drive runs its own PID"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 33",
    "name": "Running",
    "why": "Running status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3",
    "name": "Motor Speed (Motor Actual Speed)",
    "why": "Actual motor speed, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 5",
    "name": "Motor Current",
    "why": "Motor current, A"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 6",
    "name": "Output Power",
    "why": "Output power, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 22",
    "name": "Trip",
    "why": "Drive tripped"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 21",
    "name": "Warning",
    "why": "Active warning"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 61",
    "name": "Fault Status Word 1",
    "why": "Fault code word"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Parameter group 5.5 Control Places: Control Place Selection (5.5.2.1, also AV 49) must be Advanced Control or Fieldbus Control, with Fieldbus Speed Reference Source and the Advanced Start/Stop/Coast inputs set to Fieldbus.",
  "heartbeat": "BACnet Connection Timeout (10.3.7.2.14, default 60 s, 10-18000 s) watches the fieldbus data. The response (10.3.7.2.16) can be set to info, warning, warning with a switch to the alternative control place (10.3.7.2.15), or fault (ramp then coast, or coast).",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Device instance is parameter 10.3.7.2.1 (default 1, range 1-4194303); APDU segment timeout default 5000 ms and APDU timeout default 6000 ms.",
   "BACnet/IP: the X1/X2 Ethernet ports carry the fieldbus; BBMD and foreign-device registration are set through the Network Port object.",
   "BACnet MS/TP (OS7BN): baud 9600-115200, Max Masters default 32 (0-127) and Max Info Frames default 1 (parameters 10.3.7.2.2-3).",
   "A cold start resets drive parameters to factory defaults but keeps the BACnet communication settings."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Warm and cold start (ReinitializeDevice) are refused while the drive is running.",
   "Control word bits 12-15 (BV 80-83) are user-defined; their function is set by parameters.",
   "Fault Reset (BV 3) is printed read-only in the object table, so check on site whether a reset can be written over the network."
  ]
 },
